Description
Comprehensive documentation for the beast-family-service repository, detailing its non-governmental social services mission, system architecture, database schema, smart contract workflows, and Google Cloud Run deployment steps.

Core Code
Markdown
# BEAST Family Service (`beast-family-service`)

`beast-family-service` is a decentralized, privacy-focused social services division under the New World Order Private Government framework. It provides a non-governmental alternative to traditional child protective services, prioritizing family preservation, neutral domestic mediation, and secure dual-parent communication.

---

## 🏗 Repository Architecture

```text
beast-family-service/
├── contracts/               # Solidity smart contracts for family agreements
│   └── FamilyAgreement.sol  # On-chain registry for guardian pacts & milestones
├── backend/                 # Node.js Express API & PostgreSQL database integration
│   ├── src/                 # Routes, database connectors, and mediation logic
│   ├── db/                  # SQL schema definitions
│   └── Dockerfile           # Cloud Run container configuration
├── frontend/                # Next.js App Router guardian portal & intake dashboard
├── .github/workflows/       # CI/CD deployment pipeline to Google Cloud Run
└── README.md                # System documentation
🚀 Getting Started
1. Prerequisites
Node.js (>= 20.0.0)

PostgreSQL / Google Cloud SQL instance

MetaMask or compatible Web3 wallet

2. Run Backend Service
Bash
cd backend
npm install
npm run dev
3. Run Frontend Portal
Bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
🔒 Core Principles
Family Preservation: Focuses on de-escalation, mediation, and keeping families together rather than punitive state intervention.

Dual-Parent Communication: Ensures open, neutral communication channels between both guardians regardless of living arrangements.

Cryptographic Transparency: Immutable logging of mediation milestones and agreements via smart contracts on Ethereum-compatible networks.
